.TH SYNCTHINGTUI 1 "August 2026" "syncthingtui 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syncthingtui \- terminal user interface for Syncthing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syncthingtui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syncthingtui
is a keyboard-driven terminal user interface for managing a running
.BR syncthing (1)
instance, aiming for feature parity with the official Syncthing web GUI.
.PP
It allows adding/editing/pausing/resuming/rescanning of devices and folders,
system settings changes, and new device or folder offers to be accepted.
.PP
With no options,
.B syncthingtui
discovers the address and API key of the local Syncthing instance from its
.I config.xml
(see
.BR FILES )
and connects to it, polling for updated state every three seconds.
.PP
A terminal of at least 80x60 characters is recommended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-address " ADDRESS"
Syncthing GUI address, for example
.IR 127.0.0.1:8384 .
By default this is read from
.IR config.xml .
If the GUI is configured for TLS, an
.I https
connection is used; certificate verification is skipped, as Syncthing GUI
certificates are self-signed, and the API key provides authentication.
.TP
.BI \-api\-key " KEY"
API key used to authenticate to the Syncthing REST API. Defaults to the value
of the
.B SYNCTHING_API_KEY
environment variable, or, if that is unset, to the key read from
.IR config.xml .
.TP
.BI \-config " PATH"
Path to the Syncthing
.I config.xml
to read the GUI address and API key from, instead of auto-discovering it in
the default locations. Useful for a non-standard configuration directory or a
second instance.
.TP
.B \-fake
Run against built-in fake data instead of a live Syncthing instance. Useful
for trying out the interface without a running daemon.
.TP
.B \-list
List the names of the static screens accepted by
.B \-screen
and exit.
.TP
.BI \-screen " NAME"
Render the named screen statically to standard output and exit, using fake
data. Intended for layout review and testing rather than interactive use.
.TP
.BI \-size " WxH"
Terminal size, as width by height in characters, used with
.BR \-screen .
Defaults to
.IR 80x60 .
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Switch to the next or previous tab. The number keys select a tab directly.
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " Up ", " Down
Move between items in a list or fields in a form.
.TP
.B Enter
Activate the selected item, or begin editing the selected field. While editing,
.B Enter
commits the value.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q ", " Backspace
Leave the current view, or quit from the top level. While a field is being
edited,
.B Esc
cancels the edit and only then leaves the view.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/syncthing/config.xml
Syncthing configuration, read to discover the GUI address and API key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/syncthing/config.xml
Legacy location of the above, used if the first is not present.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYNCTHING_API_KEY
Default value for
.BR \-api\-key .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B syncthingtui
exits 0 on success, and non-zero if no Syncthing instance could be discovered
or contacted, or if the arguments were invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syncthing (1)
.PP
The Syncthing documentation at
.UR https://docs.syncthing.net/
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Evan Widloski.
